   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the local finance law, in relation to authorizing the town of\nNorth Hempstead to issue bonds or notes to finance certain liabilities of the\nlength of service award programs of fire companies located within the town and\nproviding fire protection to residents of the town",
    "basePrintNo": "S7084",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7084-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11.00, Loc Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Local Finance Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7084\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the local finance law, in relation to authorizing the\ntown of North Hempstead to issue bonds or notes to finance certain\nliabilities of the length of service award programs of fire companies\nlocated within the town and providing fire protection to residents of\nthe town\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would allow the Town to issue bonds or notes to finance\nliabilities of the Length of Service Award Programs (LOSAP) for fire\ncompanies located within the Town\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nParagraph 1 of section 11.00 of the local finance law is amended by\nadding a new subdivision 109 by adding payments by the town of North\nHempstead of contributions to service award programs established pursu-\nant to section 217 of the General Municipal Law for five years. Section\n2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town of North Hempstead has requested an amendment to the State's\nLocal Finance Law that would allow the Town to issue bonds or notes to\nfinance liabilities of the Length of Service Award Programs (LOSAP) for\nfire companies located within the Town. The purpose of this proposed\nlegislation will allow the Town to issue bonds or notes to finance\nexisting underfunded LOSAPs of the Albertson Hook and Ladder and Hose\nCompany No. 1 and the Floral Park Centre Fire Company No. 1. Both of the\nFire Company's' LOSAPs are currently underfunded which in effect costs\nthe Town 5.25% (the assumed rate of return required on the LOSAP invest-\nment portfolios).\n\nBy allowing the Town to issue bonds or notes to eliminate the LOSAP\nunderfunding this will ultimately reduce the LOSAP related costs for the\nTown and its residents as the interest rates associated with a new bond\nor note would be estimated at 2%. It is economically prudent for the\nTown to issue bonds at a cost of roughly 2% and use the proceeds to\neliminate the LOSAP's underfunding. The net result would be a 3.25%\nreduction (5.25%-2%) in LOSAP related costs for the Town and its resi-\ndents.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
